            <ArticleTitle>Current management of ophthalmic zoster.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>273-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Most ophthalmic zoster occurs in healthy people and ocular complications occur in 50%. The mainstay of ocular therapy is topical steroid, but careful follow-up and withdrawal are essential. The place of systemic steroid therapy and acyclovir in immunocompetent patients with zoster is uncertain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
